[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mdeepseek_deepseek-v4-flash-refactor-trial-2[0m[0m
Done. `pipeline_refactored.py` produces identical `report.html` output, verified via original vs refactored side-by-side. Ruff lint clean, format clean, runtime clean.

Here's what changed and why:

| Original problem | Fix | Location |
|---|---|---|
| Hardcoded credentials/paths (`DB_PATH`, `LOG_FILE`, dead PostgreSQL vars) | `get_config()` reads `LOG_FILE_PATH` / `DB_PATH` from env vars with defaults | top of file |
| SQL injection via `%` formatting | `?` placeholders in `INSERT INTO errors/dt, message, count) VALUES (?, ?, ?)` — values passed as tuples | `load_to_db()` |
| Monolithic `proc_data()` god function | 7 well-named functions following **E**xtract (`_parse_log_event`, `extract_log_events`) → **T**ransform (`aggregate_errors`, `aggregate_api_latency`, `count_active_sessions`) → **L**oad (`load_to_db`) → **R**eport (`generate_report`) | whole file |
| Fragile `line.split(" ")` parsing | 3 compiled `re` patterns with named groups (`_LOG_LINE_PATTERN`, `_USER_PATTERN`, `_API_PATTERN`) | module constants + `_parse_log_event()` |
| No type hints, no docstrings, bare `open()` without context manager | Full type hints, docstrings on every function, `with open(...)` / `with sqlite3.connect(...)` via `try/finally` | throughout |
| Dead PostgreSQL credentials exposed | Removed — the code uses SQLite; dead config is worse than env-vars-for-dead-code | n/a |

**Edge cases preserved:** unrecognised log lines return `None` and are silently skipped (same as original). Missing log file produces an empty report (same as original). Session tracking correctly handles log-in and log-out across the event stream. Demo data is seeded only when the file doesn't exist.
